  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Parallax Depth\n\nA layered landscape trucks sideways with a gentle push-in, near layers sliding faster than far ones. Built-in sun and hills preview on their own; a host adds its own full-frame layers by pushing an element and a depth (1 is nearest, larger moves less) onto LAYERS in the script.\n\nCategory: camera. Length: 3 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- An opener or a quiet beat needs a cinematic establishing shot, a slow sideways camera move across a sun and hills.\n- You have a few flat layers and want them to read as one scene with real depth.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The subject is a screenshot or long page the camera should travel across: use stage.\n- The subject should hold its size while the space behind it stretches: use dolly-zoom.\n\nVariables:\n- distance (number, 0-1.5): Distance, default 0.5\n- push (number, 0-0.6): Push-in, default 0.16\n- direction (enum): Direction, default \"1\"\n- sky_color (color): Sky, default \"#111111\"\n- sun_color (color): Sun, default \"#E5322D\"\n- far_color (color): Far hills, default \"#2C2C2C\"\n- mid_color (color): Mid hills, default \"#555555\"\n- near_color (color): Near hills, default \"#8E8E8E\"\n- seed (number, 1-99): Seed, default 3\n- speed (number, 0.25-3): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Parallax Depth\n\n  A layered landscape trucks sideways with a gentle push-in, near layers sliding faster than far ones. Built-in sun and hills preview on their own; a host adds its own full-frame layers by pushing an element and a depth (1 is nearest, larger moves less) onto LAYERS in the script.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/parallax-depth/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"parallax-depth\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"distance\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Distance\", \"description\": \"Sideways camera travel at depth 1, as a fraction of the frame width.\", \"default\": 0.5, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 1.5, \"step\": 0.01},\n    {\"id\": \"push\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Push-in\", \"description\": \"Push-in toward the scene, in depth units.\", \"default\": 0.16, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 0.6, \"step\": 0.01},\n    {\"id\": \"direction\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Direction\", \"description\": \"Truck direction: right or left.\", \"default\": \"1\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"1\", \"label\": \"Right\"}, {\"value\": \"-1\", \"label\": \"Left\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"sky_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Sky\", \"description\": \"Sky color.\", \"default\": \"#111111\"},\n    {\"id\": \"sun_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Sun\", \"description\": \"Sun color.\", \"default\": \"#E5322D\"},\n    {\"id\": \"far_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Far hills\", \"description\": \"Farthest hill layer.\", \"default\": \"#2C2C2C\"},\n    {\"id\": \"mid_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Mid hills\", \"description\": \"Middle hill layer.\", \"default\": \"#555555\"},\n    {\"id\": \"near_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Near hills\", \"description\": \"Nearest hill layer.\", \"default\": \"#8E8E8E\"},\n    {\"id\": \"seed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Seed\", \"description\": \"Seed for the hill outlines.\", \"default\": 3, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 99, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 3, \"step\": 0.05}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Parallax Depth</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n\n        #root { background: var(--sky); }\n        .pd-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; overflow: hidden; }\n        .pd-layer { position: absolute; inset: 0; transform-origin: 50% 55%; }\n        .pd-layer svg { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; overflow: visible; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"parallax-depth\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"pd-clip\" class=\"pd-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <!-- Layers are built in the script. A host adds its own by pushing { el, depth } onto LAYERS. -->\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var NAME = \"parallax-depth\";\n\nvar root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\nvar vars = window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables() : {};\nfunction num(v, f, min, max) { var n = Number(v); return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : f; }\nfunction str(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v.trim() ? v : f; }\nfunction col(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && /^#([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i.test(v.trim()) ? v.trim() : f; }\nfunction bool(v, f) { return v === true || v === \"true\" ? true : v === false || v === \"false\" ? false : f; }\nvar FPS = 30;\nvar DUR = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2\");\nvar TOTAL = Math.round(DUR * FPS);\nfunction lerp(a, b, t) { return a + (b - a) * t; }\nfunction cl(x, a, b) { return Math.min(b, Math.max(a, x)); }\n// interpolate(x, [in...], [out...], easing): clamped on both sides, easing applied per segment.\nfunction interp(x, inp, out, easing) {\n  if (x <= inp[0]) return out[0];\n  if (x >= inp[inp.length - 1]) return out[out.length - 1];\n  var i = 0;\n  while (x > inp[i + 1]) i++;\n  var t = (x - inp[i]) / (inp[i + 1] - inp[i]);\n  if (easing) t = easing(t);\n  return out[i] + (out[i + 1] - out[i]) * t;\n}\nfunction bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n  return function (x) {\n    if (x <= 0) return 0; if (x >= 1) return 1;\n    var t = x;\n    for (var i = 0; i < 8; i++) {\n      var cx = 3 * x1 * t * (1 - t) * (1 - t) + 3 * x2 * t * t * (1 - t) + t * t * t - x;\n      var d = 3 * x1 * (1 - t) * (1 - t) - 6 * x1 * t * (1 - t) + 6 * x2 * t * (1 - t) - 3 * x2 * t * t + 3 * t * t;\n      if (Math.abs(cx) < 1e-6 || Math.abs(d) < 1e-6) break;\n      t -= cx / d;\n    }\n    t = cl(t, 0, 1);\n    return 3 * y1 * t * (1 - t) * (1 - t) + 3 * y2 * t * t * (1 - t) + t * t * t;\n  };\n}\nvar E = {\n  lin: function (t) { return t; },\n  quad: function (t) { return t * t; },\n  cubic: function (t) { return t * t * t; },\n  sin: function (t) { return 1 - Math.cos((t * Math.PI) / 2); }\n};\nfunction eOut(f) { return function (t) { return 1 - f(1 - t); }; }\nfunction eInOut(f) { return function (t) { return t < 0.5 ? f(2 * t) / 2 : 1 - f(2 - 2 * t) / 2; }; }\nvar outCubic = eOut(E.cubic), outQuad = eOut(E.quad), inCubic = E.cubic, inQuad = E.quad;\nvar inOutCubic = eInOut(E.cubic), inOutQuad = eInOut(E.quad), inOutSin = eInOut(E.sin), outSin = eOut(E.sin);\n// Damped spring from 0 to 1 (rest at 1, no initial velocity), frames at 30 fps.\nfunction spring(frame, cfg) {\n  if (frame <= 0) return 0;\n  var m = cfg.mass || 1, k = cfg.stiffness, c = cfg.damping;\n  var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / m), z = c / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * m)), t = frame / FPS;\n  if (z < 1) {\n    var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n    return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + ((z * w0) / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n  }\n  if (z === 1) return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n  var s = w0 * Math.sqrt(z * z - 1), r1 = -z * w0 + s, r2 = -z * w0 - s;\n  return 1 - (r2 * Math.exp(r1 * t) - r1 * Math.exp(r2 * t)) / (r2 - r1);\n}\n// Seeded random: same string in, same number out.\nfunction rnd(seed) {\n  var sd = String(seed), h = 1779033703 ^ sd.length;\n  for (var i = 0; i < sd.length; i++) { h = Math.imul(h ^ sd.charCodeAt(i), 3432918353); h = (h << 13) | (h >>> 19); }\n  h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 16), 2246822507); h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 3266489909); h ^= h >>> 16;\n  var a = (h >>> 0);\n  a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a);\n  t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\n  return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n}\nfunction rgb(h) {\n  h = h.replace(\"#\", \"\");\n  if (h.length === 3) h = h[0] + h[0] + h[1] + h[1] + h[2] + h[2];\n  return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16), parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16), parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16)];\n}\nfunction mixc(a, b, t) {\n  var x = rgb(a), y = rgb(b);\n  return \"rgb(\" + Math.round(lerp(x[0], y[0], t)) + \",\" + Math.round(lerp(x[1], y[1], t)) + \",\" + Math.round(lerp(x[2], y[2], t)) + \")\";\n}\nfunction rgba(h, a) { var x = rgb(h); return \"rgba(\" + x[0] + \",\" + x[1] + \",\" + x[2] + \",\" + a + \")\"; }\nvar SVGNS = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\nfunction svgEl(tag, attrs, parent) {\n  var e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);\n  for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);\n  if (parent) parent.appendChild(e);\n  return e;\n}\nfunction setA(e, attrs) { for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]); }\n// Drive draw(frame) from the timeline; frames run 0..frames over frames/30 seconds.\nfunction drive(draw, frames) {\n  var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n  var clock = { frame: 0 };\n  tl.to(clock, { frame: frames, duration: frames / FPS, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.frame); } }, 0);\n  draw(0);\n  return tl;\n}\nfunction finish(tl) {\n  if (tl.duration() < DUR) tl.to({}, { duration: DUR - tl.duration() });\n  tl.seek(0);\n  window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n  window.__timelines[NAME] = tl;\n}\n\n\nvar stage = document.getElementById(\"pd-clip\");\nvar distance = num(vars.distance, 0.5, 0, 1.5), push = num(vars.push, 0.16, 0, 0.6), direction = String(vars.direction) === \"-1\" ? -1 : 1, seed = Math.round(num(vars.seed, 3, 1, 99)), speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0, 4);\nvar C = { sky: col(vars.sky_color, \"#111111\"), sun: col(vars.sun_color, \"#E5322D\"), far: col(vars.far_color, \"#2C2C2C\"), mid: col(vars.mid_color, \"#555555\"), near: col(vars.near_color, \"#8E8E8E\") };\nroot.style.setProperty(\"--sky\", C.sky);\nvar W = root.clientWidth, H = root.clientHeight;\nfunction hillPath(base, amp, waves, sd) {\n  var oct = [0, 1, 2].map(function (o) { return { f: (waves * (o + 1) * (0.8 + rnd(sd + \"-f\" + o) * 0.4)) / W, a: amp / (o * 1.7 + 1), p: rnd(sd + \"-p\" + o) * Math.PI * 2 }; });\n  var steps = 120, x0 = -W, x1 = W * 2, d = \"M \" + x0 + \" \" + H * 2;\n  for (var i = 0; i <= steps; i++) {\n    var x = x0 + ((x1 - x0) * i) / steps, y = base;\n    oct.forEach(function (o) { y -= o.a * (0.5 + 0.5 * Math.sin(x * o.f * 6.283 + o.p)); });\n    d += \" L \" + x.toFixed(1) + \" \" + y.toFixed(1);\n  }\n  return d + \" L \" + x1 + \" \" + H * 2 + \" Z\";\n}\nvar LAYERS = [];\nfunction addLayer(depth, fill) {\n  var el = document.createElement(\"div\"); el.className = \"pd-layer\";\n  var svg = svgEl(\"svg\", { viewBox: \"0 0 \" + W + \" \" + H }, el);\n  stage.appendChild(el);\n  LAYERS.push({ el: el, depth: depth });\n  return svg;\n}\nsvgEl(\"circle\", { cx: W * 0.6, cy: H * 0.4, r: H * 0.17, fill: C.sun }, addLayer(9));\nsvgEl(\"path\", { d: hillPath(H * 0.6, H * 0.24, 2.2, seed + \"-far\"), fill: C.far }, addLayer(6));\nsvgEl(\"path\", { d: hillPath(H * 0.76, H * 0.16, 1.2, seed + \"-mid\"), fill: C.mid }, addLayer(2.6));\nsvgEl(\"path\", { d: hillPath(H * 0.92, H * 0.14, 0.9, seed + \"-near\"), fill: C.near }, addLayer(1.2));\nvar DURATION = 60, moveEase = bez(0.45, 0, 0.2, 1);\nfunction draw(frame) {\n  var t = frame * speed;\n  var move = interp(t, [0, DURATION], [0, 1], moveEase);\n  var camX = (move - 0.5) * distance * W * direction, camZ = move * push;\n  LAYERS.slice().sort(function (a, b) { return b.depth - a.depth; }).forEach(function (l, i) {\n    var depth = Math.max(0.2, l.depth);\n    var scale = depth / Math.max(0.05, depth - camZ);\n    var x = (-camX * scale) / depth;\n    l.el.style.zIndex = i;\n    l.el.style.transform = \"translateX(\" + x + \"px) scale(\" + scale + \")\";\n  });\n}\nfinish(drive(draw, TOTAL));\n\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
